usage: measure_output_performance.py [-h] --executable LABEL=PATH --output
                                     OUTPUT [--rounds ROUNDS]
                                     [--memory-repeats MEMORY_REPEATS]
                                     [--observer OBSERVER] [--events EVENTS]
                                     [--order {legacy,blocked}]
                                     [--workload {hits,events,mesh}]
                                     [--format {csv,root,both}]

Repeatable output-format measurements; engineering timing, not a physical
benchmark.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --executable LABEL=PATH
  --output OUTPUT       new measurement directory
  --rounds ROUNDS
  --memory-repeats MEMORY_REPEATS
                        optional independent PID-bound RSS runs (requires
                        --observer)
  --observer OBSERVER   path to the preflight PID observer (only with
                        --memory-repeats)
  --events EVENTS
  --order {legacy,blocked}
                        legacy keeps the old CLI combo order; blocked rotates
                        the combo list by the repeat index and records the
                        order
  --workload {hits,events,mesh}
  --format {csv,root,both}
